WEBVTT

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:04.870
﻿Where are you!?

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.700
﻿A super long range shot!

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:16.040
﻿That's the GM Sniper K9.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.880
﻿What firing accuracy!
﻿No wonder they're in the best 16.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.260
<i>﻿But I'm better at close combat!</i>

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:38.330
﻿- Hold it for 20 seconds.
- ﻿Roger that!

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.910
﻿It's a lightweight type,
﻿but all this power!

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:54.350
﻿With that much firepower,
﻿my Abigorbine won't even—

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:01.420
﻿Wh-What!?

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.060
﻿It's over.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.570
<i>﻿Battle ended.</i>

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:22.540
﻿Mr. Luang lost...?

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:24.380
﻿To whom?

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.850
﻿So much for being a top contender.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:31.950
﻿That was a piece of cake.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:05.780
﻿That was unexpected.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:09.350
﻿Luang Dallara's been eliminated already?

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:14.890
﻿The Renato brothers haven't done
﻿anything remarkable until now.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:19.020
﻿They must have been concealing...

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:21.690
﻿their sharply honed claws.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.100
﻿But that's probably all over now.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.030
﻿Their next opponent is too tough.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:32.940
﻿What the heck!

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:37.110
﻿Everybody's talking about
﻿Meijin this and Meijin that.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.380
﻿Leave it be.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:42.550
﻿Just imagine their reaction
﻿when we beat him.

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:45.680
﻿Can't you hear it already?

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:49.820
﻿The sound of people around the world
﻿gasping in surprise.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:00.130
﻿Gunpla Shingyo School, Mao Yasaka!

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.570
﻿I'm completely revived!

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:05.470
﻿- That was quick.
- That was quick.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:08.270
﻿I have no time to mope around.

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:10.270
﻿I've figured out my problems,

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.340
﻿now I just need to move forward.

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:16.510
﻿I'm staying here until
﻿the tournament is over.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:19.920
﻿Please tell me if I can help with anything.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.520
﻿Alright. Thanks.

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:23.950
﻿By the way...

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:27.530
﻿Do you know where I'm off to now?

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:29.090
﻿Who cares?

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:32.130
﻿Wh-Where're you going, Mao?

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:37.800
﻿Actually, I'm off to
﻿the hobby center with Misaki.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.640
﻿It's a date. It's a date.

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:41.770
﻿A date!

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:46.640
﻿What was that about?

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:50.280
﻿Maybe he's cheering us
﻿up in his own way.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:51.650
﻿I doubt that.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:55.550
﻿- A date with Misaki.
- ﻿M-Maybe...

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:00.660
﻿Yasaka's on a date?

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:02.960
﻿Is he with Miss Misaki?

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:04.730
﻿Yeah, that's what he said.

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:07.530
﻿That's nice.

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:13.040
﻿Wh-When the tournament is over,
﻿m-maybe we could...

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:18.610
﻿This yakisoba looks so delicious!

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:21.810
﻿But so do those dumplings.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:25.920
﻿That's the girl Reiji was with.

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:30.620
﻿H-Hello.

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:33.620
﻿Have we met somewhere?

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:35.360
﻿Oh! I'm sorry.

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:38.760
﻿We saw you with Reiji the other day.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:41.000
﻿Reiji!?

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.030
﻿Hey!

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:45.640
﻿Sorry, I'm late.

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:50.980
﻿I'll introduce myself first.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:55.210
﻿I'm Sei Iori, a contestant in
﻿the Gunpla Battle Championship.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:58.850
﻿I'm his classmate, China Kousaka.

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:00.480
﻿Y-Yes...

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:02.050
﻿And I'm Reiji!

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:03.120
﻿That I know.

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:06.020
﻿What's your name?

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:11.230
﻿I'm Ai... Ai...

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:12.430
﻿I'm Aina.

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:17.370
﻿You have the same name as
﻿the 08th MS Team's heroine!

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:19.170
﻿R-Really?

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.840
﻿So your name is Aina?

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:24.310
﻿Didn't know that.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.540
﻿I've never told you.

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:28.010
﻿Miss Aina,

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:31.280
﻿did you come here to watch
﻿the Gunpla Battle Championship?

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.280
﻿Huh? Um... Yes...

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:37.550
﻿Didn't you say you aren't
﻿interested in Gunpla?

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:42.260
﻿M-My friend invited me.
﻿I'm just tagging along.

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:45.130
﻿Do you even have any friends?

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:47.160
﻿What do you mean?

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.000
﻿I'm saying you're rude.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.100
﻿You're one to talk!

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.470
﻿- What did you say!?
﻿- What!

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:56.470
﻿Calm down...

00:06:56.710 --> 00:07:00.110
﻿Would you like something sweet?

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:01.580
﻿- Yeah!

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:20.830
﻿Sure, joints may be fragile,

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:24.400
﻿but it's impossible to destroy them
﻿that much with handguns.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.340
﻿There are no traces of funnels or bits.

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:31.610
﻿It's like magic.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:36.010
﻿There's a cause and effect
﻿for everything.

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:38.820
﻿Even if it's sorcery or sleight of hand,

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:41.220
﻿you just need to know the trick.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:43.220
﻿You're confident.

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:45.490
﻿I'm welcoming this.

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:48.130
﻿Against them,
﻿it looks like I can fight seriously.

00:07:48.990 --> 00:07:50.790
﻿And I'll win.

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:52.860
﻿That's the mission of a Meijin...

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:55.030
﻿who has inherited the Kawaguchi name.

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:01.870
﻿And then...

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:09.310
﻿Julio, we can't afford to hold back
﻿in tomorrow's battle.

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:10.810
﻿We'll give it our all.

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:13.980
﻿There's no need for that, brother.

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:19.590
﻿Compared to the second Meijin,
﻿the third is like a child's game.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:21.390
﻿But that's why.

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:24.530
﻿We'll strip him of his glory...

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:26.830
﻿while the whole world watches.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.730
﻿Alright, brother.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:33.740
﻿Let's give them a chance
﻿to witness our battle.

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:36.870
﻿No, our war!

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:44.850
﻿This is yummy.

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:46.620
﻿Yeah, it's delicious.

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:50.890
﻿D-Don't eat too much.

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:53.990
﻿They're very much alike.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:55.960
- ﻿You say something?

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:58.030
﻿Nothing.

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:01.930
﻿Let's go get some more!

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:04.570
﻿Looks like you're having a good time.

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:07.540
﻿M-Mao!?

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:09.070
﻿Where'd you come from?

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:11.480
﻿What happened?
﻿Weren't you on a date?

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:14.480
﻿Yes, I went on a date.

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:17.410
﻿I did go on a date...

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:25.690
﻿Misaki!

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:28.590
﻿Mao!

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:30.490
﻿Misaki!

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:32.430
﻿Mao!

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:34.600
﻿Misaki!

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:36.500
﻿Mao!

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:39.300
﻿Misaki! Misaki!

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:39.940
﻿Misaki...!

00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:45.780
﻿It's too soon!
﻿I'm not ready for that!

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:48.510
﻿You should never rush these things.

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:51.110
﻿Misaki!

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:55.690
﻿Misaki... Misaki...

00:09:55.890 --> 00:09:57.150
﻿It's your fault.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:00.520
﻿So straightforward!
﻿Can't you put it differently?

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:03.460
﻿I can't. You're so insensitive.

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:05.530
﻿- Shut it for a sec!
﻿- You're so mean...

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:07.300
﻿Stop crying like a baby!

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:14.470
﻿Fellini isn't here.

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:18.240
﻿He said he'll watch it on video
﻿because Yuuki will win anyway.

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:20.010
﻿Yeah, I agree.

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:21.780
﻿And Mao?

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:24.950
﻿I'm afraid to talk to him now.

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:27.680
﻿China, where's Mrs. Rinko?

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:31.260
﻿Since Iori and Reiji
﻿don't have a match today,

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:33.060
﻿she said she'll go shopping.

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:34.730
﻿I-I see.

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:41.200
<i>﻿We now begin quarterfinals match one
﻿of the tournament finals.</i>

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:42.800
﻿Here we go.

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:43.470
﻿Yeah.

00:10:57.020 --> 00:10:59.520
﻿We'll show you our war.

00:11:00.020 --> 00:11:03.850
﻿Buckle up, Mr. Meijin.

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:12.260
<i>﻿We now begin quarterfinals match one
﻿of the tournament finals.</i>

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:15.200
<i>﻿Please set your GP Base.</i>

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:25.340
<i>﻿Beginning Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:31.720
<i>Field 7, Ruins.</i>

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:38.420
<i>﻿Battle start.</i>

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:44.930
﻿Meijin Kawaguchi,
﻿Kämpfer Amazing, launching!

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:59.480
﻿I've reached the destination.

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:04.410
﻿It's best to think that
﻿they're already able to snipe at us.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:08.190
﻿The points from where
﻿they can aim here...

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:09.590
﻿One of these three.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:11.960
<i>﻿What to do, Kawaguchi?</i>

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:14.520
﻿I won't give them
﻿any time to use their tricks.

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:16.460
﻿I'll poke at the shrubs.

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:30.870
﻿Did he spot our location!?

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:34.280
﻿Don't be panicked.
﻿It's just a diversion.

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:37.950
﻿It looks like the Meijin is
hoping for a shoot-out.

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:40.680
<i>﻿Plan S4. Send in the Hound.</i>

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:41.890
﻿Roger!

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:48.160
﻿Take off!

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:55.030
﻿Hound, start firing
﻿as soon as deployment is complete.

00:12:58.870 --> 00:12:59.400
﻿- Mr. Ral.
- ﻿Huh?

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:02.510
﻿What's he shooting at?

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:06.110
﻿His opponent is the GM Sniper K9.

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:08.710
﻿The Meijin's attacking the sniping points,

00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:11.380
﻿and trying to flush it out.

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:27.260
﻿- Deployment completed.
- ﻿Then let's begin.

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:28.100
﻿Okay.

00:13:40.850 --> 00:13:42.280
﻿- It moved!
- ﻿I'll pursue it!

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:48.750
﻿Are you serious?

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:53.760
﻿It blocked that!?

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:56.430
﻿Now I know where it is—!

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:02.500
﻿The right leg container!

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:04.940
﻿Attack from another direction?

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:07.070
﻿Self propelled artillery!

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:09.240
﻿Behind you!

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:13.910
﻿We can't go from above.
﻿Drag the opponent down.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.920
﻿- Movement confirmed.
- ﻿You won't get away!

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:41.940
﻿- A wire trap!
- ﻿In such a short time!?

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:52.780
﻿A trap!

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:55.990
﻿Gotcha!

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:06.830
<i>﻿Kawaguchi, get to the facility
﻿behind you to the right.</i>

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:07.830
﻿I have no choice.

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:15.610
﻿He fell for it, brother!

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:18.040
﻿Good. Deploy the Bloodhound team.

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:26.650
﻿We can't see from here!

00:15:26.750 --> 00:15:28.390
﻿What's going on?

00:15:28.390 --> 00:15:30.550
﻿- Let's go where we can see!
- ﻿Yeah!

00:15:34.430 --> 00:15:37.760
﻿I can't believe they
﻿brought in multiple machines.

00:15:37.760 --> 00:15:41.630
﻿When we confronted the GM,
﻿its backpack was missing.

00:15:42.630 --> 00:15:46.400
﻿They're operating it independently
﻿as self-propelled artillery.

00:15:46.770 --> 00:15:50.310
﻿But it was a good call to run in here.

00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:54.410
﻿Even if they bring in two machines,
﻿you have an edge in this tight space.

00:15:54.410 --> 00:15:59.020
﻿No, I'm suspecting that
﻿they lured us here on purpose.

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:01.080
﻿What do you mean?

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:03.190
﻿A tactician likes to use tricks.

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:05.590
﻿Keep searching for enemies.

00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:08.060
﻿I can see now!

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:10.790
﻿Yuuki's Kämpfer still looks intact.

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:12.360
﻿That's good.

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:14.360
﻿Sei, over there!

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:16.530
﻿Something small is moving!

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:17.470
﻿Something small?

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:22.270
﻿What are those?

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:25.810
﻿- What!?
﻿- What happened?

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:26.940
﻿There's something near us!

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:30.380
- ﻿Execute Operation Time Stop.
- ﻿Roger.

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:32.280
﻿Those are...!

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:35.220
﻿1/144 Zeon soldier figures!?

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:37.950
﻿They're setting
﻿time bombs on the joints!

00:16:40.420 --> 00:16:43.590
﻿Zeon soldiers!? I get it now!

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:46.300
﻿Setup is complete, brother.

00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:47.900
- ﻿Detonate.
﻿- Detonate.

00:16:50.270 --> 00:16:51.300
﻿Yuuki!

00:16:52.170 --> 00:16:54.070
﻿What happened?

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:55.940
﻿They set bombs.

00:16:55.940 --> 00:16:57.370
﻿- Bombs?
- ﻿Yeah.

00:16:58.140 --> 00:17:02.310
﻿It's probably the same tactic
﻿they used against Luang Dallara.

00:17:03.310 --> 00:17:05.080
﻿The Renato brothers...

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:08.550
﻿What they're playing isn't Gunpla battle!

00:17:09.150 --> 00:17:10.990
﻿Hound, stand by to rear.

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:12.420
﻿Have the GM charge in.

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:14.890
﻿Though it should be in pieces by now.

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:22.870
﻿He's still alive!

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:26.770
﻿How did he survive that explosion!?

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:29.010
﻿Why!? Why...!?

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:34.140
﻿This sliminess and shine...

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:35.510
﻿Grease?

00:17:35.910 --> 00:17:37.480
﻿Exactly.

00:17:37.480 --> 00:17:40.820
﻿By looking at the way
﻿Luang Dallara's Gunpla was damaged,

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:43.690
﻿we anticipated that you'd
﻿do something to the joints.

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:48.460
﻿That's why we applied
﻿slippery grease beforehand.

00:17:51.030 --> 00:17:52.830
﻿Is the magic over now?

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:55.000
<i>﻿You!</i>

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:02.040
<i>﻿Then prepare for the worst!</i>

00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:06.040
﻿What!?

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:09.650
﻿What?

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:11.480
﻿Its power suddenly increased.

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:12.620
﻿A Trans-Am system?

00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:13.780
﻿No,

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:17.190
﻿its head camera has changed
﻿from green to red.

00:18:17.960 --> 00:18:20.060
﻿That's not Trans-Am,

00:18:20.060 --> 00:18:24.060
﻿but the EXAM system developed
for use against Newtypes!

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:30.630
﻿Save your trump card till the end.
﻿That's just basic tactics.

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:31.200
﻿Go!

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:36.210
﻿It's fast!

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:51.760
<i>﻿You don't deserve the name of Meijin.</i>

00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:56.390
﻿We'll prove it to the world
﻿through this war of ours.

00:18:56.590 --> 00:18:57.960
﻿A war?

00:18:57.960 --> 00:18:59.130
<i>﻿Yes.</i>

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:04.000
<i>﻿A real battle that a peace-spoiled boy
﻿like you can't handle.</i>

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:08.170
﻿Darn! Our last weapon...!

00:19:27.190 --> 00:19:28.530
﻿- That's not good!
- ﻿President Yuuki!

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:32.000
﻿Yuuki...!

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:35.700
﻿He's going to lose...

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:40.600
﻿Our Gunpla is going to lose.

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:45.810
﻿The Gunpla that embodies
﻿all of PPSE's best technologies...

00:19:45.810 --> 00:19:46.540
﻿Allan.

00:19:46.940 --> 00:19:49.480
﻿Everyone has a fate.

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:51.950
﻿A drama without a script.

00:19:52.550 --> 00:19:55.120
﻿But this is inevitable!

00:20:00.990 --> 00:20:04.630
<i>﻿Time to give up, Mr. Meijin.</i>

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:09.130
﻿What!?

00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:34.320
﻿Th-That's impossible.

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:39.160
﻿He lured us to the spot
﻿where the container fell...!

00:20:39.430 --> 00:20:41.970
﻿It's not over!
﻿We still have the Hound.

00:20:45.400 --> 00:20:46.500
﻿A rifle!?

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:48.610
<i>﻿This is not a war.</i>

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:51.440
﻿This is Gunpla Battle!

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:54.780
﻿Kawaguchi!!!

00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:04.290
<i>﻿Battle ended.</i>

00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:13.130
﻿B-Brother...

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:16.300
﻿So this is where it ends?

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:20.370
﻿The war of the Renato brothers...

00:21:21.810 --> 00:21:23.770
﻿Thanks, Kawaguchi.

00:21:23.770 --> 00:21:27.810
﻿If you weren't the fighter,
﻿we couldn't have won this battle.

00:21:27.810 --> 00:21:29.380
﻿I'm mad at myself.

00:21:30.780 --> 00:21:33.550
﻿I damaged the machine this much.

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:37.490
﻿I've failed as a Meijin.

00:21:37.720 --> 00:21:40.590
﻿He's shown us some battle.

00:21:40.590 --> 00:21:43.390
﻿Yuuki really is amazing.

00:21:43.590 --> 00:21:46.100
﻿Otherwise, we'd lose our edge.

00:21:46.100 --> 00:21:47.830
﻿Right, Sei?

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:49.470
﻿Yeah.

00:21:50.770 --> 00:21:53.800
﻿Let's go to the place where he is!

00:21:53.800 --> 00:21:55.910
﻿Yeah!

00:23:26.930 --> 00:23:29.330
﻿I'm sorry, Chairman.

00:23:29.330 --> 00:23:30.370
﻿Yes.

00:23:30.830 --> 00:23:31.900
﻿Yes.

00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:34.140
﻿By the time you get back,

00:23:34.140 --> 00:23:36.940
﻿The Sei Iori and Reiji team
﻿will definitely...

00:23:36.940 --> 00:23:37.940
﻿Yes.

00:23:37.940 --> 00:23:39.140
﻿Goodbye.

00:23:42.350 --> 00:23:45.210
﻿They won't win this time.

00:23:46.150 --> 00:23:50.350
﻿Because their next opponent
﻿is the Early Genius...

00:23:51.890 --> 00:23:54.790
﻿the Samurai Boy.

00:23:55.880 --> 00:24:00.080
﻿I'll trust in my inner beliefs
﻿to win this battle.

00:24:00.080 --> 00:24:02.120
Next episode, "Astray's Blade".

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:04.880
This is the Gunpla Battle
that you've never experienced.
